able. You cannot debug a request that touches six services without distributed tracing. If you do not have tracing, logging, and metrics in place before you split the monolith, you will regret it.\n\nThe honest answer on whether to adopt microservices: it depends on your team size and operational maturity. A team of five engineers does not need twelve services. Start with a well-structured monolith, extract services only when you hit a specific scaling or deployment bottleneck, and make sure you can actually operate what you build.\n"}}, {"tool_name": "Skill", "tool_use_id": "toolu_vrtx_01BVCvNYuEyfTiFNy2cK1bBw", "tool_input": {"skill": "prose:pre-validator", "args": "source.md"}}], "terminal_reason": "completed", "fast_mode_state": "off", "uuid": "67af504d-46e4-4cb0-be65-b3c0d2e59f9e", "timestamp": "2026-05-04T11:58:38.995Z"}